# System libraries Chromium links against, for the heroku-community/apt buildpack.
#
# Heroku dynos have no root, so `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`
# cannot do this itself — the `--with-deps` half shells out to apt-get and
# fails. This file is that half, done at build time by a buildpack that can.
#
# Not hand-assembled. This is Playwright's own dependency list for
# ubuntu24.04-x64 Chromium, read out of the installed playwright-core bundle
# (lib/coreBundle.js, the `chromium:` array under the 24.04 table) rather than
# copied off a blog post. Heroku-24 IS Ubuntu 24.04, which is why the t64
# variants are the right ones: 24.04 renamed these packages during the 64-bit
# time_t transition, and the pre-t64 names simply do not resolve there.
#
# When Playwright is upgraded, re-read that array rather than trusting this
# file. tools/lib/ci-parity.test.ts compares the two and fails if they drift.
libasound2t64
libatk-bridge2.0-0t64
libatk1.0-0t64
libatspi2.0-0t64
libcairo2
libcups2t64
libdbus-1-3
libdrm2
libgbm1
libglib2.0-0t64
libnspr4
libnss3
libpango-1.0-0
libx11-6
libxcb1
libxcomposite1
libxdamage1
libxext6
libxfixes3
libxkbcommon0
libxrandr2

# Fonts. Not in Playwright's list, because its own CI image already has them.
# A dyno does not: without these Chromium falls back to whatever it can find,
# text metrics shift, and every rendered-page assertion becomes a coin flip.
fonts-liberation
fonts-noto-color-emoji
